Subject: [PATCH 47/50] tracker 0.10.0: the quiet mesh (SPEC 3.2, PROTOCOL.md
 2.6, 2.7, 3.3 to 3.5)

Copies 9 (zero-hop), 11 (along the stored path), 0 and 10 (floods at the scope level, one wider)
with a route per TX queue entry; the 8 s retransmission removed; floods counted only for floods.
The link policy (lt_core lt_link.c): NEAR, ROUTED, FAR, hold, moved, ack_patience, moved without
GPS by a discover at the next check, no-fix backoff, parked flood, heartbeat, the IDLE budget of 8
with next_in of the last flood, R29. The decision point 12 s after a hello (12 s + 1 s per hop
after a routed copy), copy 10 8 s after copy 0 without evidence. ACKs (near and routed, channel
and stealth) in the listen window and at every slot; early sleep after an ACK without MORE.
Schedule anchor with slots from ks, the previous grid for 3 slots after a flood, SYNC in every
report, commands at slots sealed from ks (mesh and Bluetooth). Commands under 0xFF4C and 0xFF6C,
answer timing option C (a quick answer within 2 s, also during a GPS search, which resumes), the
sticky CMD_ACK (R4). Bridge areas (4 state rows, one baked) and the ladder. Counter checkpoints at
multiples of 16, moved only on a send. Low-battery DM at the decision point (R27). Phase
deadlines: a stall ends the phase without a reset. Mode end is an event. Console: link, area,
scopetest, ackpatience, log and history flags, events link and lvl. Field log: FL_SUM1..3 per
report wake-up and FL_CHK per slot. State ext magic LT10 (a 0.9.8 state migrates). Defaults:
report every 3, still 2 24.
